@page "/demo/charts"
@using Fx.ControlKit.Charts
@using FlexCore.Showcase.Components.Shared
@* 2026-10-12: wrapped in FeatureDemoLayout as one example (the tabbed gallery, unchanged). "No JavaScript
   dependencies" reworded per the claims rule. ChartControl parameter table pending (SC-264).
   2026-10-20: ?tab=<slug> opens the gallery on that tab (catalog row Sparkline Charts); slugs in TabSlugs.
   2026-10-29: nine more tiles (ComboBarLine, RangeBar, StepLine, MultiLine, RangeArea, HighLow, Pyramid, DotPlot, ArcGauge), so every
   ChartType with a renderer is drawn on this page or on Financial & gauges.
   2026-10-23 (developer meeting point 5, label clutter): every SVG chart draws on a fixed viewBox (600x300; 300x300 for
   Pie, Donut, Radar, Gauge; 400x300 for Funnel) with xMidYMid meet, so rendered text = tile scale, and a tile taller
   than its width-bound height is blank. Each layout now sets CellAspectRatio so a tile is title + chart (+ legend)
   tall, and every Height is the width-bound value (226px in a 453px two-column tile, 400px full width). Dense charts
   (Histogram, Box Plot, Waterfall, Pareto, Funnel) have full-width tiles; Part-to-Whole went from 3 to 2 columns with
   the Sunburst on a SizeY=2 row that holds its 680px drawing. Scatter and Bubble put numeric x values in Label (the
   renderer parses Label as x and draws no x tick labels). Radar "JavaScript" -> "JS" (labels cut at 8). Waterfall is
   deltas only: the renderer adds every point to the running total, so "Gross Profit"/"Net Income" subtotal bars were
   drawn as further increases. Funnel values and stage names chosen so each label fits its segment. Heatmap legend
   hidden (it repeated the row labels). Gantt has 8 tasks so the rows fill the plot (rowH is capped at 30 units).
   YAxis Max/TickCount set where the default 1.1 x max gave ragged tick values. HorizontalBar has no renderer (draws
   as Bar) and is not used. The Stacked Area title and the Sunburst itself are untouched. 
   2026-10-24: Documentation written as eleven tables from Charts/ChartControl.razor, ChartModels.cs, ChartEnums.cs, ChartControl.razor.css and
   ChartSvg.cs (rows in ChartsVocab.*.cs, checked with scratchpad/vocabcheck.py; read sites, not just declarations).
   2026-10-24: the datasets became small stories (ice cream flavours, a bakery's week, two seedlings growing, a favourite-colour
   survey, a library front desk, an office coffee machine); every title names its subject, series and categories are real words,
   and the 2026-10-23 geometry (label cuts, tile sizes, every YAxis Max) is unchanged. The data is made up.
   2026-10-25 (Baaria): charts that have a page of their own left the gallery: the Sunburst panel (Part-to-Whole), the three
   ChartType.Gauge tiles (KPI & Gauge, now "KPI cards") and the Project tab (ChartType.Gantt). The Overview and Related list point at
   those pages. ChartType.Gauge and ChartType.Gantt are now drawn on no page (the gauge and Gantt pages use the dedicated controls);
   their ChartType rows say so. TabSlugs follow the tabs: kpi-gauge became kpi, project went. *@

<PageTitle>Blazor Charts (Line, Bar, Pie, Area, Scatter) — FlexCore</PageTitle>

<FeatureDemoLayout Title="Charts" Category="Charts" CategoryHref="demo/charts" ControlName="ChartControl"
                   Tagline="One control, 35+ chart types, drawn in SVG from C#."
                   SourcePath="Charts/ChartControl.razor;Charts/ChartModels.cs;Charts/ChartEnums.cs;Charts/ChartControl.razor.css;Charts/ChartSvg.cs">
    <Overview>
        <p>
            <code>ChartControl</code> takes a <code>ChartType</code> and a list of <code>ChartSeries</code> and draws the result as SVG;
            there is no npm package or third-party script behind it. The gallery groups the types by the question they answer:
            comparison, trend, part-to-whole, distribution, correlation, multivariate, KPI cards, statistics, heatmap and sparklines.
            Charts with a page of their own are not repeated here: the drill-down <a href="demo/charts/sunburst">sunburst</a>, the
            <a href="demo/gantt">Gantt chart</a>, the <a href="demo/gauges">gauges and stock chart</a> and the <a href="demo/charts/map-story">map story</a>;
            candlestick, OHLC, bullet, range, Sankey and the radial and linear gauge types are on <a href="demo/advanced-charts">Financial &amp; gauges</a>.
        </p>
    </Overview>

    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Id="gallery" Title="Gallery by purpose" RazorCode="@Code.Gallery" CSharpCode="@Code.GalleryCs">
            <Description><p>Every chart here is the same control with a different <code>Type</code>. Series data is bound; titles, heights, axes, legends and palettes are parameters.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
<TabControl @bind-SelectedIndex="_tab">
