    <Vocabulary>
        <p>
            One control, one data shape. <code>Type</code> picks the renderer; <code>Series</code> carries the data as
            <code>ChartSeries</code> of <code>ChartDataPoint</code>, whose <code>Value2</code> to <code>Value5</code> mean different things
            per type; <code>XAxis</code>, <code>YAxis</code> and <code>Legend</code> hold the optional axis and legend settings. Every SVG
            type draws on a fixed canvas (600 by 300 units for most types) scaled to fit the width it is given, and its label text is a
            fixed size in that drawing, so a chart in a narrow tile has small labels and a wide one has large labels. Each row below says
            which types read the setting; a row marked never read is declared in the library but has no effect yet.
        </p>
        <DocSections>
            <DocSection Id="doc-chartcontrol-parameters" Title="ChartControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(ChartsVocab.Params.Length, "parameters")' Open="true">
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="ChartControl parameters" Rows="ChartsVocab.Params" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-gauge-and-kpi-parameters" Title="Gauge and KPI parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(ChartsVocab.GaugeKpi.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="Gauge and KPI parameters" Rows="ChartsVocab.GaugeKpi" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-charttype" Title="ChartType" Count='@DocSection.Label(ChartsVocab.Types.Length, "values")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Values" Title="ChartType" Rows="ChartsVocab.Types" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-chartseries" Title="ChartSeries" Count='@DocSection.Label(ChartsVocab.Series.Length, "properties")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="ChartSeries" Rows="ChartsVocab.Series" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-chartdatapoint" Title="ChartDataPoint" Count='@DocSection.Label(ChartsVocab.Point.Length, "properties")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="ChartDataPoint" Rows="ChartsVocab.Point" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-chartaxis" Title="ChartAxis" Count='@DocSection.Label(ChartsVocab.Axis.Length, "properties")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="ChartAxis" Rows="ChartsVocab.Axis" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-chartlegend" Title="ChartLegend" Count='@DocSection.Label(ChartsVocab.Legend.Length, "properties")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="ChartLegend" Rows="ChartsVocab.Legend" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-chartcontrol-chartbar-the-legacy-bar-lis" Title="ChartControl.ChartBar, the legacy bar list" Count='@DocSection.Label(ChartsVocab.Bar.Length, "properties")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="ChartControl.ChartBar, the legacy bar list" Rows="ChartsVocab.Bar" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-chartsvg-the-same-renderer-as-a-string" Title="ChartSvg, the same renderer as a string" Count='@DocSection.Label(ChartsVocab.Methods.Length, "methods")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Methods" Title="ChartSvg, the same renderer as a string" Rows="ChartsVocab.Methods" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-css-classes" Title="CSS classes" Count='@DocSection.Label(ChartsVocab.Css.Length, "classes")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.CssClasses" Title="CSS classes" Rows="ChartsVocab.Css" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-css-variables" Title="CSS variables" Count='@DocSection.Label(ChartsVocab.CssVars.Length, "variables")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.CssVariables" Title="CSS variables" Rows="ChartsVocab.CssVars" />
                <p>
                <code>ChartControl</code> raises no events and has no public methods. <code>GaugeRange</code> and <code>GaugePointer</code>,
                used by <code>GaugeRanges</code> and <code>GaugePointers</code>, are documented on the <a href="demo/gauges">Gauges &amp; stock chart</a>
                page; <code>SunburstChartControl</code>, which the <code>Sunburst</code> type delegates to, on the <a href="demo/charts/sunburst">Sunburst</a> page.
